  "question": {
    "text": "Two metal strips are riveted together at their ends by four rivets, each of diameter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mtext>mm</mtext></math>. Assuming that each of the rivets carries one-quarter of the load, the maximum tension that can be produced in the riveted strip is [Breaking shear stress of the rivet = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>.9</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Pa</mi></math>]"
